spectrace/ngram.py contains a Python port of _find_longest_matched_ngram_and_propose_tokens from vLLM
(vllm-project/vllm, vllm/v1/spec_decode/ngram_proposer.py), Apache License 2.0, Copyright contributors to the vLLM project.

The offline estimator of expected speculative-sampling rounds used here was published first by Zhao and Cai,
arXiv:2610.10411 (2026-10-07); related counterfactual drafter evaluation: Liu et al., "Not-a-Bandit", arXiv:2510.20064.
This repository contributes engine validation, RL drafter-selection experiments and an engine conformance check (see REPORT.md).

Models used (not redistributed): Qwen2.5-0.5B, Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct, Qwen2.5-Coder-0.5B-Instruct, Qwen2.5-1.5B, Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct,
Qwen2.5-Math-1.5B-Instruct (Qwen team, Apache License 2.0); hkust-nlp/Qwen-2.5-1.5B-SimpleRL-Zoo (Apache License 2.0).
Data: openai/gsm8k (MIT). tests/vllm_ngram_30_requests.json contains token IDs of prompts written for this project and of outputs
generated by Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct with vLLM 0.31.0. Kaggle usernames in results/logs are redacted as <kaggle-user>.
